{{!--
  Dragonbane — the ONE definition of a card illustration.

  Two callers, one partial:

    • front.hbs, for its two picture places (placement="front")
      → {{> card-image url=(slot "front-image-top" image=true) alt="" placement="front"}}
    • the engine, for every `![[bild.png]]` in a note's body, at exactly the
      spot it stands there (placement="body") — in practice the generic
      card, the one Dragonbane card type that renders note markdown.

  The WRAP belongs to the face and must NOT go into the text flow.
  `.db-front-image-wrap` is `flex: 1 1 0` with a `min-height` — the flex
  slot of the body column. Set between two paragraphs, the picture would
  take every pixel the text leaves over. What carries over is what really
  makes the design: the borderless seat (`cs-front-image`) and the soft edge
  (`fade-edges`).

  The cap therefore has to be restated for the body form: `.db-front-image`
  caps at `max-height: 100%` — "100 % of the wrap", and without a wrap that
  measures against an indefinite height, exactly the value the FontScaler's
  two passes disagree about. `.db-body-image` in dragonbane.css sets an
  absolute length instead.
--}}
{{#if (eq placement "body")}}
<img class="db-front-image db-body-image cs-front-image fade-edges" src="{{url}}" alt="{{alt}}" />
{{else}}
<div class="db-front-image-wrap">
  <img class="db-front-image cs-front-image fade-edges" src="{{url}}" alt="{{alt}}" />
</div>
{{/if}}
